+### Clickable nodes with labels (avoid text overlay stealing events)
+
+Common failure: for marks like bubbles/nodes, a `<text>` label is drawn on top of a `<circle>` and **intercepts pointer events**, making hover/click unreliable.
+
+Robust, reusable structure:
+```js
+const node = svg.selectAll('g.node')
+  .data(nodes, d => d.id)
+  .join(enter => {
+    const g = enter.append('g').attr('class', 'node');
+    g.append('circle').attr('r', d => d.r);
+    g.append('text')
+      .text(d => d.label)
+      .attr('text-anchor', 'middle')
+      .attr('dy', '0.35em')
+      .style('pointer-events', 'none'); // critical
+    return g;
+  });
+
+node
+  .style('cursor', 'pointer')
+  .on('mouseover', (event, d) => { /* tooltip */ })
+  .on('mouseout',  (event, d) => { /* tooltip hide */ })
+  .on('click',     (event, d) => { /* selection */ });
+```
+
+Guidelines:
+- Prefer binding events to the parent `<g class="node">` so circle+label behave as one target.
+- Ensure label has `pointer-events: none` (via CSS or `.style(...)`).
+
+### Bidirectional linking (chart ⇄ table) pattern
+
+When the task includes both a chart and a table/list, use a **single source of truth** and one update function.
+
+Reusable pattern:
+```js
+let selectedId = null;
+
+function updateSelection(id) {
+  selectedId = id;
+
+  // chart marks
+  node.classed('selected', d => d.id === selectedId);
+
+  // table rows
+  rows.classed('selected', d => d.id === selectedId);
+}
+
+node.on('click', (event, d) => updateSelection(d.id));
+rows.on('click', (event, d) => updateSelection(d.id));
+```
+
+CSS example:
+```css
+.node.selected circle { stroke: #111; stroke-width: 3px; }
+tr.selected { background: #ffe9a8; }
+```
+
+Acceptance checklist for linked interactions:
+- Clicking a mark highlights the corresponding row.
+- Clicking a row highlights the corresponding mark.
+- Clicking directly on the label text still triggers the mark interaction (label does not steal events).
+
